Gold's common version comparator is derived from the MIT-licensed ShutUp
implementation. Legacy NITTC Scheduler and GlyphVisualizer/Glyph Barty
algorithms are retained as test fixtures. Elief's notification layouts draw
on the MIT-licensed Scheduler and ShutUp UI. Source revisions and the
BeastLocator comparison research are recorded in
docs/four-app-updater-comparison.md; historical characterization results
remain in docs/phase-2-core-report.md.

Gold and Elief are ordinary AARs; third-party dependencies are resolved
transitively rather than shaded into them. Their licenses remain applicable.
See docs/third-party-licenses.md.
